# PLAN 3.4 matrix: OptTarget SPOT x Zernike (OptZern mode 12) DOF (CC 2026-10-11; the programmatic twins are
# tCalibMatrix / test_calib_matrix.py, TO).  The deck (tst_calib_zern.in) is spoiled: ANSI mode 12 (Z(4,0)) 2e-7 m;
# CALIB must remove the spoil, print its merit and say why it stopped.  SPOT is the deck's own
# target; WFE / ZWF are selected through SETP (SETP offers WFE, ZWF and Beam -- not SPOT).
# DEADLINE: 120
# COPY: $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_calib_zern.in
old $DECK
calib
no
yes
show 1
# EXPECT: Final LM merit \(chisq\) =\s+\S+
# EXPECT: Stopped: 
# EXPECT-NOT: Optimization aborted
# EXPECT-NOT: singular
# EXPECT: ZernCoef=\s+(0\.0E\+00|-?\d\.\d+E-(09|[1-9]\d))
# (measured 2026-10-11 at 338416c, both compilers: every cell stops at the cap T=10; TIP -> <= 1.8e-9, h^4 -> <= 3.3e-9, Z12 -> <= 5.5e-17)
